# module `headset_gates`: each rule of src/quest/combat/headset_gates.cpp, headset_gates.h, headset_gates_targets.h and combat_gates.h removed or bent once; the
# module's host tests (src/quest/tests/headset_gates_test.cpp; combat_gates_test.cpp and headset_gates_library_name_test.cpp where a mutant names them)
# must fail on every one. Sourced by ../mutants.sh, which defines `runm <name> <file> <sed> [<build dir> <test target>]`.
# Run: src/quest/combat/mutants.sh headset_gates
#
# The three rules are the three gates: gate_perm (the party-permissions caller), gate_bots (the bot-body caller, only where levelname is installed and a combat
# map or the combat lobby is loaded) and gate_link (the menu Bind, answered per script library). The first mutants of each section are the rule itself; the rest
# are its counters, its lines and its refusals.
#
# Not listed, because no host test can tell them from the original:
#   - `slot == 0` in LevelNameInstalled, and `ok &&` after it: an unpublished or unreadable slot gives a word of 0, which `word != 0` already refuses.
#   - `!*readable ||` in FirstWordMismatch: an unreadable word reads 0, which differs from every pinned word.
#   - `if (!known) return false;` in LinkLibAnswered: a library that cannot be named is the empty string, which no fragment is a part of.
#   - the `continue` in SetLinkGateLibs's "none" branch: it ends the loop body, so removing it changes nothing; the branch itself is mutated below.
#   - `len < kFragmentLen` in SetLinkGateLibs when moved to `<=`: a stored 48-character fragment can never be a part of a library name of at most 47 characters.
#   - `g_levelNameSlot.store(0)` after a refused headset slot: with no entry on the slot nothing calls the continuation that reads it.
#   - the arm64 entries' own instructions: check/headset_gates.sh runs them under qemu.
F=src/quest/combat/headset_gates.cpp
H=src/quest/combat/headset_gates.h
T=src/quest/combat/headset_gates_targets.h
G=src/quest/combat/combat_gates.h
LN=quest-host-combat
